  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: A dry start to the day, but moderate to perhaps \nheavy rain expected later today into early Sunday.\n\nExpect showers and storms to form later this afternoon into\nSunday morning, as warm advection brings back the more humid\nairmass.\n\nThis will be followed by more showers and storms later Sunday\nafternoon and evening, as stronger dynamics and cold front\nwork on the humid airmass. \n\nNot a lot cold advection, abnormally warm and moist air\ntake aim at the Great Lakes area again on Tuesday, as a\nstrong upper level ridge builds northward from the TN Vly.\n\nERO for today adjusted to one area, and SPC outlook for \nSunday trimmed across the southeast. Complex fcst, as been\nthe case this summer.\n\nStill holding off on a flood watch for now, given nothing\ngoing on yet on radar, still time to see how things play out \nlater this aft. \n\nMore information below.\n\nGuidance does put numerous heavy bands of rain over the area. \nFFG lower west and north, but heaviest QPF could be to the\neast. Also maybe things more an issue later Sunday, depending\non where that rain falls today. \n\nAgain, the problem is: where? With uncertainty high as it is \nand FFG getting higher slowly, still holding off.",
